# Component Architecture

## Section module layout

Every page section is its own folder under `src/components/<SectionName>/` containing:

```
HomeOfferShowcase/
├── HomeOfferShowcase.tsx   ← composing root, named export
├── OfferSectionHeader.tsx  ← sub-pieces
├── OfferCard.tsx
├── OfferCardsRail.tsx
├── OfferCarouselNav.tsx
├── OfferInquiry.tsx
├── OfferFooterNotch.tsx
└── constants.ts            ← copy, items, Figma node IDs
```

Rules:

- One default-free named export per file matching the filename.
- Root component is data-driven; all copy/imagery comes from a typed `Props` object. `constants.ts` provides the static fallback used by `homeStatic` seed today and the Payload block tomorrow.
- Sub-components must be reusable: e.g. `OfferCard` knows nothing about "home" — it accepts `title`, `description`, `imageSrc`, `cropClassName`.
- Client state (refs, scroll, listeners) lives in the smallest possible leaf with `'use client'`. The composing root should remain a Server Component whenever possible.

## Props

- `Props` types named `<Component>Props`, defined just above the component.
- Use `readonly` arrays / `as const` for static option lists.
- Booleans are positive (`isActive`, not `notActive`).
- Avoid optional chained renders deep inside JSX; precompute in variables for readability.

## Reuse boundary

Generic primitives (`OczkiButton`, layout grids) live in `src/components/<Primitive>/`. Section-specific compositions live inside the section folder. Do not move section-specific files into shared folders.
